# VenCom E2E testing (`y-tst-e2e-vencom`)

**Entry point** for VendorCOM end-to-end runs. This rule does **not** copy runbooks — it links to repo docs and shared `y-rules`. Feature sub-rules (for example owner report) add the **how** for their layers.

Final report: `.cursor/rules/y-rules/insight/y-ins-e2e-report.mdc`.

**Direct invoke:** if the user already named a sub-rule (e.g. `/y-tst-e2e-vencom-owner-report`), still run **this** pre-flight first, then follow the sub-rule.

Do **not** invent work-order ids. Use ids from the MP API response, the simulator run, a harness fixture, or user-supplied verified values.

---

## Mandatory pre-flight (AskQuestion only)

**Do not start any E2E step until applicable questions are answered.**

### Q0 — Test-docs

Check whether `docs/<JIRA-KEY>/test-cases.md` exists, **or** a user-chosen ticket path such as `docs/tickets/<JIRA-KEY>/test-cases.md` (`NO-TICKET` → skip to Q1). Use the path the user named for the shared report; do not force `docs/<KEY>/` when they already chose another folder.

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Create criteria and cases first** (recommended when missing) | Follow `.cursor/rules/y-rules/test/y-tst-testing-criteria.mdc` then `.cursor/rules/y-rules/test/y-tst-test-cases.mdc`. Resume this rule after the files exist. |
| **Run without them** | Continue. The shared report **skips** its QA (`-qa.md`) file. Detailed and Compact still required. |
| **Stop** | Do not start the run. |

When the doc exists (including `docs/tickets/<JIRA-KEY>/`), execute **every case** in it **in document order**. Skip cases that do not match Q1/Q2; record **Not run** with the reason. This rule does **not** define cases.

### Q1 — Environment

| Option | Stack |
|--------|--------|
| **Local MP** (recommended when a local Marketplace runs on this machine) | Local Marketplace API + its RabbitMQ; VenCom `BASE_URL` / `RBTMQ_*` point at them. Start and stop stacks with the machine's local gateway scripts when they exist, not with ad-hoc `docker compose` calls. |
| **Local (simulator)** | `docker-compose.yml` + `docker-compose.test.yml` — see [docs/testing/local-manual-scenarios.md](../../../docs/testing/local-manual-scenarios.md) |
| **MP Testing (marketplace mode)** | Marketplace-wired stack — see [docs/operations/test-harness.md](../../../docs/operations/test-harness.md) and [docs/testing/harness-e2e-scenarios.md](../../../docs/testing/harness-e2e-scenarios.md) |

### Q2 — Driver

| Option | When |
|--------|------|
| **Manual MP API** | Local MP only — create the work order and service through the MP API, approve VenCom drafts in MP, inject participant replies per `.cursor/rules/y-vencom-rules/test/y-vencom-inbound-payload.mdc` |
| **Manual simulator API** | Local simulator only — `publish-init` / `inject` / `inject-raw` on `:8090` |
| **Harness canned scenario** | `e2e_*` health checks (UI, CLI, or JSON API) |
| **Harness directed aim** | Director drives the conversation from a plain-language aim |
| **Render only (report_pdf CLI)** | PDF content without the swarm (`python -m subprojects.report_pdf.cli`) |

**Blocked:** simulator API on anything but Local simulator; Manual MP API on anything but Local MP; marketplace-mode harness on a simulator-wired stack. The harness Mode must match how the stack was started.

